<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hasta Siempre, Comandante</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1965">1965</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Hasta Siempre, Comandante&quot; (&quot;Until Forever, Commander&quot;), often simply &quot;Hasta Siempre&quot;, was written in 1965 by the Cuban composer Carlos Puebla. Its words answer the farewell letter that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/che-guevara">Che Guevara</a>, a commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuban-revolution">Cuban Revolution</a>, left when he departed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> to spread revolution in the Congo and later in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a>, where he was captured and killed.</p></div>
